\n- For graphs II and  III, some horizontal lines intersect the curve more than once. So, these are not one-to-one functions. As a result, they are not invertible."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186403244 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a8c6b41-dda4-5b72-b40c-3e85cba087db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403246} {:answer/id #uuid "8c44c0b8-a324-51aa-8160-2529aa798669" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403247} {:answer/id #uuid "f2ff6185-1935-54af-a0dd-0d7567723234" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403248} {:answer/id #uuid "22145362-fe93-590d-8788-5b69cf80e6c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403249} {:answer/id #uuid "5297b063-4a7c-5a1f-aec3-8f8e6212d515" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403250}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5297b063-4a7c-5a1f-aec3-8f8e6212d515" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403250} :answer-field/id #uuid "6127ad12-ca4b-5bf9-9f70-8f5bdf2f9c6d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403245}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1d080acd-916c-5650-8a33-fa75e4ad9891" :question/math-academy-id "q-66509" :question/problem "![](images/be/be5b7625ad6f540f6769b121f52ccad69b669dbf764fc3bb68f89c99f066f145.png)\n\nWhich of the graphs above correspond to an invertible function?" :question/worked-solution "A function is invertible if and only if it's a one-to-one function. To determine which of the functions are one-to-one, we use the horizontal line test.\n\n![](images/bf/bfc7d94de67ceeb0c4aaa0988c117fce7f15242c2f3d223eecd8f0eb77135d7e.png)\n\nFrom the above, we see that: \n\n- For graph IV, a horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line. Therefore, graph IV shows a one-to-one function. This means that  the function is invertible.\n\n- For graphs I, II and  III, some horizontal lines intersect the curve more than once. So, these are not one-to-one functions. As a result, they are not invertible."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186403251 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5a79b73a-03f6-5533-acf7-b5a1df8567d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403253} {:answer/id #uuid "8f1c26d9-e125-518f-bb45-e4c39ea28969" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403254} {:answer/id #uuid "168d57eb-da99-5a01-9c14-4caceb4907e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403255} {:answer/id #uuid "a58e69ca-7b57-5342-91cd-29668910ad83" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403256} {:answer/id #uuid "18db7e36-ba98-517a-818f-12aea00ad73c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403257}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a58e69ca-7b57-5342-91cd-29668910ad83" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403256} :answer-field/id #uuid "ff70fd34-fe3d-556f-9676-12869b9e2163" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403252}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e687e18c-9edd-57ea-b75b-3cb3764012f6" :question/math-academy-id "q-66514" :question/problem "![](images/f6/f65062d48189401ba22b1b08637d187eed532d5f93dca7663c2e80743510d5d7.png)\n\nWhich of the graphs above correspond to an invertible function?" :question/worked-solution "A function is invertible if and only if it's a one-to-one function. To determine which of the functions are one-to-one, we use the horizontal line test.\n\n![](images/cc/cc31f6f291058c7890a9210d5ebfac21cdd961c74c3db5e080d7fca334102b53.png)\n\nFrom the above, we see that: \n\n- For graph III, a horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line. Therefore, graph III shows a one-to-one function. This means that the function is invertible.\n\n- For graphs I, II and IV, some horizontal lines intersect the curve more than once. So, these are not one-to-one functions. As a result, they are not invertible."}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Invertible Function From Its Graph"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124473 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124284 :question/id #uuid "b6722faa-6069-59c1-8861-75b8207b0a90" :question/math-academy-id "e-3962" :question/problem "![](images/d9/d965e0b1087ad45206dd9259c963609f556bf5803af47ab18006bf40dffb2557.png)\n\n     \n\nOn which of the following intervals is the function $f(x)$ (shown above) invertible?\n\n- $(-3,-1]$\n\n- $(0,4]$\n\n- $[-2,2)$" :question/worked-solution "A function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test.   \n\n- The given function is invertible on the interval $x\\in (-3,-1].$  Indeed, any horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](images/24/245484a6a77160a5f5892738a7e1f8e488f6df8e4ba990bbc94ae964c3305525.png)\n\n- The given function is **not** invertible on the intervals $(0,4]$ and $[-2,2)$ because some horizontal lines will intersect the curve more than once.\n\n![](images/47/4737a1460e1abd4edc200404407fef10761f038d9a29e52ba0f8c3e8c69bb93f.png)\n\n          \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I  only\"."} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ffd143c8-a993-5d0b-85a5-821d6482ae60" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124951 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07090fc8-c92c-5618-9012-cf0f1646450c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321202} {:answer/id #uuid "0fe1e716-191b-5261-a643-11dccd52c0cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321272} {:answer/id #uuid "7058d824-9a65-5aad-a618-ec1279c82cf4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322025} {:answer/id #uuid "8b8f2599-68f2-5e06-b402-e4e77d2f9558" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322263} {:answer/id #uuid "c5538761-3933-52cf-bf3a-e8775a2d4878" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322679}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7058d824-9a65-5aad-a618-ec1279c82cf4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322025} :answer-field/id #uuid "2700a4d9-d130-5eeb-a944-7092bfe21365" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323244}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b8099f21-9137-5121-a075-a61a4c5ae84b" :question/math-academy-id "q-36039" :question/problem "![](images/93/936cea1e20ef7bbc1eb66acf9dd564c61476f5bb68ee05e553b00aaf3f970dc3.png)\n\nOn which of the following intervals is the function $f(x)$ (shown above) invertible? \n\nI. $x\\in [-4,0]$\n\nII. $x\\in (-4,-2]$\n\nIII. $x\\in (-3,1)$" :question/worked-solution "A function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test.  \n\n- The given function is invertible on each of the intervals $x\\in [-4,0]$ and $x\\in (-4,-2].$ Indeed, any horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](images/a4/a4499c2d4995c09b9ab6f8852cc2982f415f1650d65429c86df83800344106f4.png)\n\n- The given function is **not** invertible on the interval $x\\in (-3,1]$  because some lines will intersect the curve at more than one point.\n\n![](images/cb/cb0a462b3af10d15bb586f127baac45a74eecd5dc19848bda23664e75de968a4.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125021 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4caea11f-484f-50a4-a520-52df284329ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321753} {:answer/id #uuid "54e75cb9-e5b0-5ea8-9eaf-304e5de715df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321816} {:answer/id #uuid "888f7548-fc8c-5732-aae9-9e3aa70555ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322236} {:answer/id #uuid "c304d552-6f05-5067-a107-0c7b855a1c17" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322661} {:answer/id #uuid "f99f1c2f-bc18-5796-a3e2-28f9f9b5b60a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323112}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "888f7548-fc8c-5732-aae9-9e3aa70555ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322236} :answer-field/id #uuid "9392c5de-5972-51d1-8356-6d7fe3ba1f53" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323456}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e891cfb3-f978-5b44-b8bf-4d4f9f71b503" :question/math-academy-id "q-36941" :question/problem "![](images/3c/3cbdac583a4cdf1b5eb761892934516a0b4edd1487bd402ae0014859c4a0ad53.png)\n\nOn which of the following intervals is the function $f(x)$ (shown above) invertible?\n\nI. $x\\in (-2,0]$\n\nII. $x\\in (-2,2]$\n\nIII. $x\\in [-4,-2]\\cup [2,4]$" :question/worked-solution "A function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test.\n\n- The given function is invertible on the interval $x\\in (-2,0].$ Indeed, a horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](images/d7/d7c6e8d314483ad67e89ce5d4675b7af27fa08c88a4ed9d95eed9ad2a4da51cc.png)\n\n- The given function is **not** invertible on the intervals $x\\in (-2,2]$ and $x\\in [-4,-2]\\cup [2,4]$ because some horizontal lines will intersect the curve more than once.\n\n![](images/ce/cee829f7e3d5f32b0acb54cb5c40406d8391d2a2967c68df0c1f5e1cae87d729.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186244150 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8a67559d-addc-5876-99c8-ffb6d43e13cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242399} {:answer/id #uuid "ae606f3c-1812-5bcb-a043-69199517528f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242701} {:answer/id #uuid "b239dedd-5240-5006-925c-8feeaa088239" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242732} {:answer/id #uuid "b91d295c-9a41-578b-8f80-c0a2065a1bcc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242802} {:answer/id #uuid "f5e89b66-1ace-5449-81d5-084cc4530eaf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243355}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ae606f3c-1812-5bcb-a043-69199517528f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242701} :answer-field/id #uuid "6d7a48f1-3b1a-5b5a-b83e-453b380ca9e2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243653}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "15f88305-1592-5719-98bf-9e054cd03fe2" :question/math-academy-id "q-108667" :question/problem "![](images/81/811ead4928d2f245235736dce473d121261ea358ca4ff3a0cc8b01bb2e9f3b31.png)\n\nOn which of the following intervals is the function $f(x)$ (shown above) invertible?\n\n- $x\\in (-3,3)$\n- $x\\in [1,4]$\n- $x\\in (-\\infty ,-3]$" :question/worked-solution "A function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test.\n\n- The given function is invertible on the interval $x\\in (-\\infty ,-3].$ Indeed, any horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](images/32/32f1ad5bdec30951900a1c30c2996ea040e65880f859c43769faf374db06a2f0.png)\n\n- The given function is **not** invertible on the intervals $x\\in (-3,3)$ and $x\\in [1,4]$ because some horizontal lines will intersect the curve more than once.\n\n![](images/8e/8ed451b24fa83de513f4a1b5c79d39f94add784c6b7265e765a3381e7b03363a.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186244151 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "279da22c-19b1-5086-a040-dce3988e373f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241522} {:answer/id #uuid "28af5b6a-ec80-5434-84ba-585ca4ac1e30" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241534} {:answer/id #uuid "72f07cff-ecee-5f92-bf4e-fda1da9687dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I  and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242198} {:answer/id #uuid "ba28cb7c-7151-538c-9e4c-a41046e4cc6e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242811} {:answer/id #uuid "bd39c47f-6760-5968-963e-cf5dd744cf25" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I  and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242842}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "72f07cff-ecee-5f92-bf4e-fda1da9687dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I  and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242198} :answer-field/id #uuid "da9636fa-9a09-5a3e-a643-ed5e797baaf4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243817}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "35a0e892-6583-50a3-a3c1-b86c3920f28b" :question/math-academy-id "q-108673" :question/problem "![](images/3d/3db32ea943ff1f457704a29f325a592eb4e1e0e53ee258041d08346bf9da4716.png)\n\nOn which of the following intervals is the function $f(x)$ (shown above) invertible?\n\n- $x\\in (-2,0]$\n- $x\\in (-3,0)$\n- $x\\in (0,2)$" :question/worked-solution "A function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test. \n\n- The given function is invertible on the intervals $x\\in (-2,0]$ and $x\\in (0,2).$ Indeed, any horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](images/46/46e1daf2cb9025b6a736f223fbe168ea32b66302cebea23ca3a2d473e78b77b3.png)\n\n        \n\n- The given function is **not** invertible on the interval $(-3,0)$  because some horizontal lines will intersect the curve more than once.\n\n![](images/d2/d2ed3670f7c67d60c7739ee35d66943b8341b2a49faa97546242609dd39afabc.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186244165 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7aba0040-ed79-59d5-8f0c-1da6506dcb09" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in [-3,5]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242260} {:answer/id #uuid "990dc71b-54dd-525d-99c9-150abcb5fde6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in [-3,1]\\cup (3,5]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242517} {:answer/id #uuid "a34d8087-ba76-52a1-b9de-dc8c243066f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in [-3,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242609} {:answer/id #uuid "bc11acb5-2479-5b6f-8d5c-5023dd267a04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in [1,5]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242829} {:answer/id #uuid "d159698e-637b-5ec8-b7bd-777c6c74a47b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in [0,5]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243023}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "990dc71b-54dd-525d-99c9-150abcb5fde6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in [-3,1]\\cup (3,5]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242517} :answer-field/id #uuid "c24403e2-8bbf-51d7-83c0-df91fa667cef" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243783}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c8649e7a-85fc-57ea-9a08-e015b963b698" :question/math-academy-id "q-108791" :question/problem "![](images/4f/4fec1c187ae2eaaf40461775425b31d896bdc63bc99233277d6f6bac8949315d.png)\n\nDetermine the largest domain on which the function $f(x)$ (shown above) is invertible." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the domain of our function is $x\\in [-3,5].$ \n\nA function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test.\n\n- The function $f(x)$ does not pass the horizontal line test on the interval $x\\in (1,3).$ In this case, the horizontal line $y=1$ intersects the graph at more than one point.\n\n![](images/eb/eb544795c61be7dd87568e6def10fc907c3554b603c3b344f88ac2a8ff847f8d.png)\n\n- Among the given options, the largest domain on which the function $f(x)$ is invertible is $x\\in [-3,1]\\cup (3,5].$ On this domain, any horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](images/40/4059a1ad684023640358af6ee38f0967957336578eb93b3299c9c842e7ce108f.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $x\\in [-3,1]\\cup (3,5].$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186244166 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ca8803d-d3a1-5a90-b629-eaffa681a751" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-2,4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241421} {:answer/id #uuid "748d7234-22b6-51f3-aa22-b25cfd94da75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in [0,4]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242216} {:answer/id #uuid "75a09077-b272-55f9-9ec5-02e4cb5e59f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (0,4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242225} {:answer/id #uuid "874dd0bf-adab-5f92-915f-11ce125271a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in [-2,0]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242365} {:answer/id #uuid "b8117842-6e5d-53d4-bbd5-db19b3700bb3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in [-2,4]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242796}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "748d7234-22b6-51f3-aa22-b25cfd94da75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in [0,4]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242216} :answer-field/id #uuid "7223ab10-697e-58e6-b5d8-13b63f336aac" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243661}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a8e69af0-0327-53e8-9129-272172fb2aff" :question/math-academy-id "q-108795" :question/problem "![](images/de/def2afaad6d1f74ca3ac8833ed6e35efea1296b324ef5a14c2d9513983a63456.png)\n\nDetermine the largest interval on which the function $f(x)$ (shown above) is invertible." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the domain of our function is $x\\in [-2,4].$\n\nA function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test.\n\n- The function $f(x)$ does not pass the horizontal line test on the interval $x\\in [-2,0].$ In this case, the horizontal line $y=-2$ intersects the graph at more than one point.\n\n![](images/03/033b9e827caf4fc89d4b179c769f5115254c811953f93caf33d0959bfd063235.png)\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is invertible on the interval $x\\in [0,4].$ On this interval, a horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](images/4c/4c91aa95131758065b1d8befe7c69895dc51d2f984a04cc8f06932a32e552792.png)\n\nTherefore, the largest interval on which the function is invertible is:\n\n$$\nx\\in [0,4]\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323736 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "59011896-39e7-52bf-8261-a97745a7ea6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321848} {:answer/id #uuid "9083ca4f-1840-5d1f-bbd0-a3aebcfb6ef3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322293} {:answer/id #uuid "947fb86d-b16d-5151-bc45-bfff1a5ca857" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322327} {:answer/id #uuid "d5d93329-76ba-546c-ae25-7c267f4496a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322815} {:answer/id #uuid "e83b1617-67a3-5666-a040-d549cf9c83ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322967}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9083ca4f-1840-5d1f-bbd0-a3aebcfb6ef3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322293} :answer-field/id #uuid "a08cc063-fbcd-53b1-b1a1-f8bf94126e53" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323480}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "69ab5c8f-74d2-578a-ab14-a3f834908b70" :question/math-academy-id "q-36002" :question/problem "![](images/c5/c51c5a4de562e5a3301ea76afc6af57b459acd4c46e5c65d54afc226d883a137.png)\n\nOn which of the following intervals is the function $f(x)$ (shown above) invertible?\n\n- $x\\in (-3,0]$\n- $x\\in (-3,1)$\n- $x\\in [0,3)$" :question/worked-solution "A function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test. \n\n- The given function is invertible on the intervals $x\\in (-3,0]$ and $x\\in [0,3).$ Indeed, a horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](images/00/00a80dde24ca012e0282362224c8b63764f5e149a8bfcda9c76ff4eb958fa93a.png)\n\n \n\n- The given function is **not** invertible on the interval $x\\in (-3,1)$  because some horizontal lines will intersect the curve more than once.\n\n![](images/9e/9ea54918e2ef4310b58e9cf8a0c9b1f9757a404d97dbbfd9e5b037af2193f38c.png)\n\n \n\nHence, the correct answer is 'I and III only''."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323737 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7739ff43-c68c-58ca-8bbe-3cf898ab85f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322081} {:answer/id #uuid "8d033687-0dda-5d24-a50d-81609e131df6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322273} {:answer/id #uuid "8f052679-93df-563a-8c3a-49901beaf19d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322283} {:answer/id #uuid "cc2a112f-a59c-5195-8734-7545ee263058" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322736} {:answer/id #uuid "eefd406f-e3a9-51c3-9df4-f6d2a447cae1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323031}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eefd406f-e3a9-51c3-9df4-f6d2a447cae1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323031} :answer-field/id #uuid "661e0d23-dac0-58fe-aeb6-82bf0e4b60b3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323373}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "544516cf-cdec-5de8-af07-1ff7e5be101e" :question/math-academy-id "q-36004" :question/problem "![](images/15/1597ad53471d0d9b44812c5caa31bcb160cfa150d1df9a9314447fa49e62ccff.png)\n\nOn which of the following intervals is the function $f(x)$ (shown above) invertible?\n\nI. $x\\in [-6,0]$\n\nII. $x\\in [-6,4)$\n\nIII. $x\\in [4,10)$" :question/worked-solution "A function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test.  \n\n- The given function is invertible on each of the intervals $x\\in [-6,0]$ and $x\\in [4,10).$ Indeed, any horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](images/7c/7cb282e3fa66af801ff03816973d5f5f1d0cb41e39d08a8addd27d7aa9c5b9df.png)\n\n      \n\n- The given function is **not** invertible on the interval $[-6,4]$  because some horizontal lines will intersect the curve more than once.\n\n![](images/00/000953609a7b3e13ad09473ead62f96aa895c7f94aa618884e69883595004fd4.png)\n\n \n\n Therefore, the correct answer is \"I  and III only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323739 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d4a999d-ad52-54bc-9609-1a635cfc7e5c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321250} {:answer/id #uuid "348fd450-639f-5e56-82a6-c291897db931" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321546} {:answer/id #uuid "39986b82-2ab5-5a5f-86db-e904841e01c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321585} {:answer/id #uuid "755404f4-77ec-54b2-be4e-0c0e2010bde8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322061} {:answer/id #uuid "f4f1bbb5-62b5-5d66-98b9-4e12a9d81779" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323068}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "348fd450-639f-5e56-82a6-c291897db931" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321546} :answer-field/id #uuid "df2fd798-c90d-5e86-9792-5a4f0ef3841a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323615}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f06fc453-0309-58aa-ad2f-fecdd1ab38c4" :question/math-academy-id "q-36008" :question/problem "![](images/27/279c3cd6084423d913186f4ba467ea50d0f794cf54773785777cb8841f5c2ca1.png)\n\nOn which of the following intervals is the function $f(x)$ (shown above) invertible?\n\n- $x\\in (-3,-1]$\n- $x\\in [-1,3]$\n- $x\\in [0,1]$" :question/worked-solution "A function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test. \n\n- The given function is invertible on the intervals $x\\in (-3,-1]$ and on $x\\in [0,1].$  Indeed, a horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](images/03/0388335095ed530ce07d278f82be5eb3bff14859db64b6e9ec47da27861bb657.png)\n\n    \n\n- The given function is **not** invertible on the interval. $x\\in [-1,3]$  because some horizontal lines will intersect the curve more than once.\n\n![](images/52/522b5661aaf9b7640c305b8cefd06f49cc8eed590f3ae736fc6720e6165bc3a9.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323742 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "014f6668-666f-5040-a144-715105254126" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321160} {:answer/id #uuid "26c34079-b0a6-5fc3-9a77-ee93f052ff20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321452} {:answer/id #uuid "80353f56-f611-551a-b4e9-abf19a92d1af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322153} {:answer/id #uuid "968df320-cd19-54ac-b971-d412835fd3ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322348} {:answer/id #uuid "f59bf802-b4bc-54f8-8889-7338410f2cd0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323072}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "80353f56-f611-551a-b4e9-abf19a92d1af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322153} :answer-field/id #uuid "28b86894-2e1c-5167-ac3e-a4dd5b6514f1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323253}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d31db013-e3f7-5fe2-aefa-8428da418673" :question/math-academy-id "q-36011" :question/problem "![](images/b0/b02c2e94e144935f0ff96846cd51b5a969fa8f884a7ca1d09abb231b7c945232.png)\n\nOn which of the following intervals is the function $f(x)$ (shown above) invertible? \n\nI. $x\\in (-4,-2)$\n\nII. $x\\in [-2,3]$\n\nIII. $x\\in [-3,3]$" :question/worked-solution "A function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test.  \n\n- The given function is invertible on each of the intervals $x\\in (-4,-2)$ and $x\\in [-2,3].$ Indeed, any horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](images/53/53fe88780b2ccb7522d2f1baa711162ec99300c2a2d4da29bba9ca532026cd07.png)\n\n- The given function is **not** invertible on  the interval $x\\in [-3,3]$  because some lines will  intersect the curve at more than one point.\n\n![](images/63/63cee4fc05ab17a8e69d9bfae578fa83c24d73e4677065a54a33a25e0871e718.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323747 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2dbc8c33-86dd-598e-8ee7-fa04f2bc7ca3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in [-3,4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321504} {:answer/id #uuid "3b34c587-aba0-515e-a326-983fc0c9bb25" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in [1,4]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321602} {:answer/id #uuid "8b61890c-a1b7-5b5d-ab2c-68b1c461cf55" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in [-3,1]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322259} {:answer/id #uuid "c42fd510-9a4e-5f4a-8ea1-cce741552a32" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in [-3,4]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322670} {:answer/id #uuid "fed6c880-f715-5a34-9e47-e4d3b005ddd0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in [-3,0]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323158}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8b61890c-a1b7-5b5d-ab2c-68b1c461cf55" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in [-3,1]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322259} :answer-field/id #uuid "bcfb24cc-9668-58dd-abc6-31788a668fce" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323537}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "6425603b-0808-58ba-b2d2-92cbdbcccb68" :question/math-academy-id "q-36061" :question/problem "![](images/4d/4d4353286b5d1668d2a67539db8b1fd27227872b1f5a2eaa5fd6015716f255b0.png)\n\nDetermine the largest interval on which the function $f(x)$ (shown above) is invertible." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the domain of our function is $x\\in [-3,4).$\n\nA function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test.\n\n- The function $f(x)$ does not pass the horizontal line test on the interval $x\\in [1,4).$ In this case, the horizontal line $y=-1$ intersects the graph at more than one point.\n\n![](images/a7/a709558673202ef4a7835dcea6e23b7ec5b13684272c56023058223c01fb8061.png)\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is invertible on the interval $x\\in [-3,1].$ On this interval, a horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](images/5a/5a65e71f571e9510580ba5fe105a6eac48acfe4564c5a6bf76371c2bf09ff651.png)\n\nTherefore, the largest interval on which the function is invertible is:\n\n$$\nx\\in [-3,1]\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323749 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34ede2f9-bcb4-564f-a5fc-a28d1e65b9ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321552} {:answer/id #uuid "52f7ae88-6bed-5e9e-8c6b-6cc3cca014d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321801} {:answer/id #uuid "62d24ea0-f0bb-5ac7-acd6-d7c6a113ce1c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321918} {:answer/id #uuid "6f3f310a-5ce6-582f-90a1-56d84b1b111c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322008} {:answer/id #uuid "770ff454-1196-5009-93b5-e58b99517c99" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322077}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "34ede2f9-bcb4-564f-a5fc-a28d1e65b9ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321552} :answer-field/id #uuid "889396dc-e947-54a7-be54-7f27632807e4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323439}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "6815ae09-6f05-5b7b-9ca9-f709c3e26769" :question/math-academy-id "q-36066" :question/problem "![](images/e2/e2065775ae6372e8c820b5e2f19f6f105e032dcd37db1e32e04af5bfa6a4faf9.png)\n\nOn which of the following intervals is the function $f(x)$ (shown above) invertible?\n\n- $x\\in (-3,-2]\\cup (2,4)$\n- $x\\in (0,2]$\n- $x\\in [1,4)$" :question/worked-solution "A function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test. \n\n- The given function is invertible on the intervals $x\\in (-3,-2]\\cup (2,4)$ and $x\\in (0,2].$ Indeed, any horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](images/3c/3c5bc724ee29aee7bef2790012bf0e73ce1ed087134213dbad36a670fd136a36.png)\n\n        \n\n- The given function is **not** invertible on the interval $[1,4)$  because some horizontal lines will intersect the curve more than once.\n\n![](images/03/03b9d70513a4ef99b39c9f05d0c0ac803f8e5611d0967015e9c1d9c0f45bd418.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I  and II only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323865 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e20f583-3b3c-51e6-b82e-2ccc2000d416" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321254} {:answer/id #uuid "3ad80893-e7cb-5571-97c4-c1cd0c6d8fe3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321598} {:answer/id #uuid "c8beff1a-6215-5b4a-bf70-d86711e70331" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322708} {:answer/id #uuid "ca60dd58-db8e-5b3a-b1a3-858f41145f9b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II  only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322720} {:answer/id #uuid "dc9d27fe-1dd4-5c9f-b2f0-ea2392051629" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322871}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ca60dd58-db8e-5b3a-b1a3-858f41145f9b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II  only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322720} :answer-field/id #uuid "12a2c0a3-5ca7-5d20-ab2b-550d6d727732" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323205}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2b24e31b-6e93-5c8b-93d0-5c6b5852eeb3" :question/math-academy-id "q-36934" :question/problem "![](images/1e/1eccd6630b69558f8a86f8336e9f0e49f37ffb29acf4a3c8f58be34346b4c93c.png)\n\nOn which of the following intervals is the function $f(x)$ (shown above) invertible?\n\n- $x\\in [-2,0]$\n- $x\\in (-3,-2]$\n- $x\\in (-3,-1]$" :question/worked-solution "A function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test. \n\n- The given function is **not** invertible on each of the intervals $x\\in [-2,0]$  and $x\\in (-3,-1]$ because some horizontal lines will intersect the curve more than once.\n\n![](images/d8/d8cc826df6fed7a4106539d88ffa8a1fdc0529904497c2d5413f9761acaccd12.png)\n\n        \n\n- The given function is invertible on the interval $x\\in (-3,-2].$ Indeed, any horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](images/bc/bc00ed8f4bdf03b248dbd9a1651ed073e352d512b830139505fba3b60e05e7e9.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \" II only\"."}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Intervals on Which a Function is Invertible Given Its Graph"}]}
